## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/cloudnoise3d.html
- Summary (EN): Cloud Noise 3D generates puffy, billowy noise in 3D space, useful for cumulus-style cloud patterns. Unlike Bubble Noise, its output is non-periodic.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Cloud Noise 3D produit un bruit gonflé et non périodique, adapté aux nuages de type cumulus.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: representative layer that sets output image size and metadata", "pos (optional): layer or VDB supplying the position at each pixel where noise is evaluated"]

- Key parameters: ["Amplitude: multiplies the noise before the Center offset", "Center: offsets the output value range", "Element Size: world-space size of the base noise element, with per-component scale", "Offset: shifts the noise function in world coordinates", "Noise Type: Simplex or Curl (divergence-free)", "Max Octaves, Lacunarity, Roughness: fractal layering controls", "Distortion: warps the noise toward decreasing or increasing values", "Stretch: stretches noise along each world axis, recommended over Element Size", "Droop / Droop Direction: bends the pattern toward a direction", "Fold Each Octave: remaps each layer so negative valleys become positive peaks", "Post Processing (in order): Fold, Complement, Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast, Clamp Minimum and Maximum"]

- Caveats: ["Output can exceed the usual range (negative values and values above 1); use the Post Processing clamps", "Complement is only reliable for values between 0 and 1"]

